<title>UK: LME de-lists three zinc brands.</title>
<headline>LME de-lists three zinc brands.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The London Metal Exchange (LME) said on Thursday that it is de-listing three brands of special high-grade zinc, which will not be deliverable against its contract after January 16, 1997.</p>
<p>The zinc brands are BBU E-ZINC of Austria, RCA of France, and Three Diamonds of Japan, the LME said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 8080</p>
